# System spec

When application code changes, check whether the system documentation must change too. There are two sources, and the on-site viewer, PDF, and Word export are generated from them:

- Developer specification: `src/docs/SRS_Regivim_System.md`
- User guide: `src/docs/UserGuide_Regivim.md`

Update the developer specification when technical implementation, architecture, data models, business logic, permissions, or system behavior changes.

Update the user guide when user-facing features, workflows, or usage instructions change.

Update both when a change affects technical behavior and what a user does or sees.

Preserve each file's existing structure, heading style, and level of detail. The developer specification stays technical. The user guide stays short, declarative, and non-technical, in its numbered chapter form. Document only behavior that is actually implemented. Do not edit either file for unrelated cleanup, rewording, or version notes the change did not require.

```markdown
<!-- A new permission that changes who can open a screen -->
<!-- Update SRS_Regivim_System.md (roles and access) and UserGuide_Regivim.md (who sees what). -->

<!-- A refactor that does not change behavior, screens, or data -->
<!-- Leave both documents unchanged. -->
```
